From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: voidforge <voidforge@valuz.io>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 15:56:53 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] openarc: embedder: client-certificate picker drawn by the
 shell

Plan C25 (C12 follow-up). OpenArcContentBrowserClient answered every
client-certificate request with "no certificate", since Chrome's picker
needs a Browser window. Chrome's own policy now runs again
(ChromeContentBrowserClient::SelectClientCertificate: the
AutoSelectCertificateForUrls setting picks without asking), and when the
user has to choose, ShowSSLClientCertificateSelector's embedder hook (the
previous patch) hands the choice to the bridge:

- OACClientCertificateRequest (OACDialogDelegate.h): "host:port" and the
  matching keychain identities (subject, issuer, expiry, DER) for the tab's
  dialog delegate (-tab:selectClientCertificate:).
- Choosing one acquires its private key (macOS may ask to allow access) and
  continues the handshake with it; Cancel, or dropping the request,
  continues without a certificate, as Chrome's dialog does; the network
  stack remembers either for the host for the session.
- SSLClientAuthObserver links prompts for the same host (answering one
  answers the others, which are withdrawn); the tab closing aborts the
  request; content's cancellation callback withdraws it.
